# PHY-030 — target independence and predictive economy

**Scientific status: PASS_CONDITIONAL_PREDICTIVITY; FUNDAMENTAL_SOURCE_PREDICTIVITY BLOCKED BY PHY-013.**

## Unfrozen theory space is too flexible

PHY-012 proves that D12+PSD+centering+rank seven leaves ten support families and, even after selecting the FIN support plus trace, three continuous spectral shape degrees of freedom. The single-cell core also does not select:

- cell graph/support;
- edge-strength ratios;
- retained-mean versus full-p or another interaction functional;
- dynamics/mobility/inertia;
- physical scale anchors and control dictionaries.

Allowing these to vary after seeing a target would make the extension non-falsifiable. Complexity penalties can prefer one fit but cannot turn that preference into a source law.

`PHY-013` therefore remains a real open atom: no target-blind parent construction has yet predicted a held-out operator/interaction relation across carriers.

## Frozen conditional submodel is predictive

A sharply frozen submodel is different:

- strict A7 is taken as the reference effective operator rather than rederived;
- PM-001 retained-mean coupling is fixed;
- a bounded-degree/cycle support family is fixed;
- `g,kappa` are obtained from independent controls rather than held-out pair/triple statistics;
- the dynamics is named before dynamic scoring.

Under that freeze the model predicts, without extra parameters, pair/triple correlations, causal-depth behavior, continuum low-mode scaling and dynamical response appropriate to the chosen rule. PHY-029 supplies three concrete held-out static observables and a preregisterable model-comparison sample budget.

Thus the conditional model has non-tautological consequences even though the fundamental selection of the model remains open.

## Comparison classes

1. PM-002 full-p coupling: same isolated core and zero-coupling limit, different pair/triple predictions.
2. dense/global support: same cell core, different propagation/locality and no cycle continuum under the same scaling.
3. Metropolis/Barker/gradient/inertial dynamics: same or related statics, different kinetics.

These alternatives ensure that success of the frozen PM-001/cycle model can be scored against real controls rather than against an unconstrained null.

## Decision

Promote **conditional predictive economy** only. Do not promote a fundamental source/uniqueness claim until SO-PHY-012-01 / PHY-013 succeeds target-blindly. If empirical work later requires retuning graph, interaction class or calibration functions separately for each held-out observable, the current prediction ID fails rather than expanding post hoc.
